Subject: AmigaOS: entry point, listener and inetd socket from the port

On AmigaOS main() is port/amiga_main.c; Dropbear's main() becomes
amiga_dropbear_main() and, without -i, calls the port's listener
amiga_listener() in place of main_noinetd(), which needs fork().
main_inetd() serves the connection in amiga_session_fd (the socket the
listener handed over with -S, or descriptor 0 from a superserver) instead
of a fixed 0, passes the listener's pre-authentication socket as the
childpipe, and skips setsid(). libnix's signal() accepts only numbers 1-6
and has no sigaction(), so only SIGINT (raised by libnix for Ctrl-C) gets a
handler; SIGTERM, SIGPIPE, SIGCHLD and SIGSEGV do not exist on AmigaOS.

